1
00:00:00,640 --> 00:00:03,070
Let's discuss about Android architecture.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,030
The Android system architecture is divided into five layers, as you can see in this diagram, from

3
00:00:20,030 --> 00:00:21,110
top to bottom.

4
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:28,490
First comes the application layer, which contains the system apps and the normal application, and

5
00:00:28,490 --> 00:00:35,660
then comes the application framework layer or the Java API framework layer, which contains all these

6
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:42,800
managers, activity managers, location manager, package managers, etc. And then comes the system

7
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:48,170
runtime layer which contains a Native C, C++ libraries and the Android runtime.

8
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:54,650
And after that, the hardware abstraction layer or the HAL, which contains the necessary logics for

9
00:00:54,650 --> 00:01:02,480
audio, bluetooth, camera sensor, etc. And at the bottom most we have the Linux kernel layer, but

10
00:01:02,490 --> 00:01:10,790
we have the drivers for audio bind to display, iPad, Bluetooth, etc. and at the bottom we have the

11
00:01:10,910 --> 00:01:12,200
power management.

12
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:15,800
So these are the five layers of Android architecture.

13
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:18,980
Let's dig deeper into each of these components.

14
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:29,380
In the application layer, both built in applications and not system level applications exists, but

15
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:34,900
they are basically responsible for more and better connection with the users and they are usually developed

16
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:41,080
in Java or Kotlin and these apps are mostly developed by the application developers.

17
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:48,820
And also there are the building stock apps which comes as part of a being to look at these system apps

18
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:51,780
or the stock apps in a later session.

19
00:01:53,410 --> 00:01:59,500
The Application Framework layer provides developers with the APIs needed to develop applications.

20
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:05,170
This layer is written in Java and it can be also called Java framework.

21
00:02:05,380 --> 00:02:10,060
But nowadays there are some frameworks written in Kotlin ask for them.

22
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:17,470
We usually develop the applications, I mean the Android applications that can call the APIs provided

