So first we have the activity manager.

26
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:35,280
So activity manager is mainly responsible for managing the lifecycle of each application.

27
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:40,530
So each application is built with different activities or fragments.

28
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:48,600
So it is the responsibility of the activity manager to manage the lifecycle of each application or each

29
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:50,760
activity within the application.

30
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,710
Next is the location manager.

31
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:59,010
The location manager provides the geographic location and positioning functions are resource.

32
00:02:59,310 --> 00:03:04,860
For example, the maps will be using the location manager to get the current location of the device.

33
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:06,150
Package Manager.

34
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:11,430
Package Manager manages all applications installed into Android system.

35
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:18,720
It's basically responsible for installing and installing and giving permissions with the applications

36
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:20,430
installed in the Android system.

37
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:21,750
Notification Manager.

38
