Notification Manager allows the application to display custom prompt information in the status bar.

39
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:34,650
So for example, when you get an email, for example, in the Gmail app, you get a message added at

40
00:03:34,650 --> 00:03:40,170
the notification that you have an email that is done through the notification manager and then comes

41
00:03:40,170 --> 00:03:41,400
the resource manager.

42
00:03:41,610 --> 00:03:47,880
It provides various non code resources that application user such as the localized to strings, pictures,

43
00:03:48,270 --> 00:03:51,180
layout files, color files, etc...

44
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:57,300
So if you are from an Android application development background, you definitely know localized strings,

45
00:03:57,300 --> 00:04:00,750
pictures, loud files, color files, exemplary to use.

46
00:04:01,170 --> 00:04:03,060
While developing the Android application.

47
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:07,320
So it is the responsibility of the resource manager to maintain it.

48
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:09,210
Then comes the telephony manager.

49
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:18,120
It manages all mobile device functions like the SIM management and the network management, etc. Then

50
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:24,270
comes to window manager, window manager managers, all the open windows.

51
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:28,620
So each activity is basically built with a window.

52
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:35,130
So we will learn more in more detail about Windows in a later session that we discuss about the Windows

53
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:36,060
management system.

54
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:42,720
And then providers and then providers allow data to be shared between different applications within

55
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:43,290
