BSD stands for Berkeley Software Distribution.

73
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:05,790
And this is specially customized for embedded Linux based devices.

74
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:08,040
And then we have the media framework.

75
00:06:08,110 --> 00:06:15,870
So this contains the library which supports recording and playback of various commonly used audio and

76
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:19,590
video formats like M.P. three, MP four, etc...

77
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:21,630
And then we have the squirrel light.

78
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:24,630
This is a lightweight, relational database engine.

79
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:28,950
This, again, a lightweight solution created for mobile devices.

80
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:33,750
And then we have is still and still stands for Simple Graphics Library.

81
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:38,450
So this is the underlying 2D graphics rendering engine for Android.

82
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:42,450
And then we have SSL, this very common security protocol.

83
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:49,470
So the sector socket layer is a security protocol that provides security and data integrity for network

84
00:06:49,470 --> 00:06:50,280
communication.

85
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:52,260
And then finally, we have the free type.

86
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:56,130
This is basically to manage the different varieties of fonts.

87
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:59,370
So this is basically a portable font engine.

88
00:06:59,670 --> 00:07:04,920
It provides a unified interface to access a variety of font file formats.

89
00:07:05,190 --> 00:07:12,510
So these are some of the major C C++ libraries found in Android system runtime layout.

90
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:18,900
The runtime library is divided into core library and ATA early stands for Android runtime.

91
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:20,670
The code library provides small.

92
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:27,930
Most of the Java language gold library functions so that developers can use the Java language to write

93
00:07:27,930 --> 00:07:29,070
Android applications.

94
00:07:29,130 --> 00:07:35,400
So the purpose of code library is to simply provide Java language code library functions.

95
00:07:35,850 --> 00:07:42,570
Now, regarding the Dalvik virtual machine or API, dalvik virtual machine can be compared with Java

96
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:48,990
virtual machine, but the Dalvik virtual machine is specifically customized for mobile devices.

97
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:56,910
It allows multiple instances of virtual machine to run in the limited memory simultaneously, and each

98
00:07:56,910 --> 00:08:01,230
Dalvik application is executed as an independent Linux process.

99
00:08:01,350 --> 00:08:09,390
So since we have separate process, it prevents all programs from closing when the virtual machine crashes.

100
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:12,750
So that is the main advantage since we have different process.

101
00:08:12,990 --> 00:08:20,670
Even if the virtual machine is virtual machine crashes, then it will prevent from all the apps or the

102
00:08:20,670 --> 00:08:22,440
programs from being closed.

103
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:30,390
So the reason why Dalvik virtual machine was migrated to RB is that they are to provide some advantages

104
00:08:30,390 --> 00:08:32,450
compared to dalvik formation.

105
00:08:32,610 --> 00:08:39,420
So under Dalvik, the bytecode needs to be converted into machine code by a just in time compiler every

106
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:41,280
time the application is run.

107
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:45,540
So Dalvik basically used a just in time compiler.

108
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:50,400
So whenever the application runs, it has to convert the code information code.

109
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:56,490
This will slow down the programming efficiency of the application because whenever the application starts

110
00:08:56,490 --> 00:09:00,510
up, it has to be first converted information code and then run the app.

111
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:05,040
This will actually slow down the execution speed of the app.

112
00:09:05,310 --> 00:09:08,940
With the introduction of RB after Android file.

113
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:16,170
The code of all the application will be pre compiled in the mission code when it is first installed

114
00:09:16,170 --> 00:09:16,950
in the device.

115
00:09:17,190 --> 00:09:20,670
This makes the application a true local application.

116
00:09:20,850 --> 00:09:27,540
In this way, Arity makes the app execute faster compared to Dalvik.

117
00:09:28,750 --> 00:09:31,390
Now let's look at the hardware abstraction layer.

118
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:37,300
The hardware abstraction layer is the interface between the operating system kernel and the hardware.

119
00:09:37,390 --> 00:09:43,150
Its purpose is to abstract the hardware to protect the intellectual property rights of the hardware

120
00:09:43,150 --> 00:09:44,140
manufacturers.

121
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:51,970
It hides the hardware interface, details of a specific platform and provides a virtual hardware platform

122
00:09:51,970 --> 00:09:56,240
for the operating system so that it has hardware independence.

123
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:59,620
It can be transplanted on various platforms.

124
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:06,760
From the perspective of software and hardware testing, both software and hardware testing can be completed

125
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:12,970
based on the hardware abstraction layer, making it possible to perform software and hardware testing

126
00:10:12,970 --> 00:10:13,810
in parallel.

127
00:10:14,050 --> 00:10:20,140
So in layman's term, a bypass of hardware abstraction layer is to control the hardware.

128
00:10:21,780 --> 00:10:26,760
But let's look at the Linux kernel layer, which is the bottom most layer in Android.

129
00:10:26,850 --> 00:10:33,330
Android ecosystem services are dependent on the Linux kernel and some Android specific drivers.

130
00:10:33,330 --> 00:10:40,500
For example, audio display, keypad, Bluetooth, USB, etc. have been added on this basis.

131
00:10:40,770 --> 00:10:48,390
The Android System Security Memory Management Process Management Network Protocol Stack and driver model

132
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:54,720
depends on this Linux kernel, which makes Android in a way more secured and stable.

133
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:57,810
So that's about the Android architecture.

134
